5. Error Decomposition in Main Theorem

```
Total MSE of Transition Law Estimation
          |
          |-- C1 * N^(-2/(2+d_Z_eff))   : Curse of dimensionality (nonparametric rate)
          |
          |-- C2 * r_N^2                : State estimation error (filtering bias)
          |
          |-- C3 * delta_max^2          : Observability deficit (structural bias)
          |
          |-- C4 * sigma_eps^2          : Measurement noise (irreducible)
          
Key message: Terms 3 and 4 do NOT vanish with sample size N -> infinity.
Therefore, collecting more data of the same type cannot overcome fundamental
unobservability or sensor noise. Structural changes (new sensors, mechanistic
constraints) are required.
```

